            <div xml:id="d567">

                <pb facs="0702" n="590" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg590"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.515/569: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul at Nanking</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Atcheson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-05-29T19:00:00-04:00">May 29, 1935—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>43. For the Minister. Your 103, May 15, 2 p.m., and Department’s 39, May 22, 7
                    p.m. Treasury Department requests information whether Chinese Government desires
                    to avail itself of the offer outlined in the Department’s telegram under
                    reference.</p>
                <p>Please report promptly by naval radio.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
